{
  "configuration_id": "config_006",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (multimodal, scgpt+imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) achieves 0.542 acc but only marginally beats RNA-only config_036 (0.530 acc, 0.515 F1), and actually loses on F1 (0.483 vs 0.515). This suggests the current weighted fusion strategy may not be effectively combining the two modalities. Question: config_006 isolates the fusion mechanism by switching from weighted to concat while keeping everything else identical (scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, multiprofile). This is the cleanest single-variable ablation from our best result. Why this experiment: With 7 experiments remaining, I need to determine whether multimodal fusion can meaningfully outperform RNA-only before investing in more complex variants (transformer aggregation, different encoders). If concat fusion improves accuracy/F1, it validates the multimodal direction and guides subsequent experiments toward better fusion+aggregation combos. If it doesn't, the bottleneck is elsewhere (aggregation or image encoder), and I can pivot. Expected cost: similar to config_001 (~2.9 GPU hours), since the architecture is identical except for the fusion layer."
}

